# Current events in town, by region, part two: Larkfield and the downs, Coldwater on Glasswater, Mirebridge in the
# fens, Southmeadow among the fields, Oakhaven in the Warmwood, and the Ridgemere Watch on the city walls.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Larkfield

scene et_wm_theft_sheep
when topic=crime kind=theft region=larkfield
a : Rustlers on the downs again. {victim} lost six head. | {victim}'s flock came back short by a dozen. | Somebody's driving stolen sheep east by night.
b[herder] : I'll sleep out with mine and my crook. Let them try.
b[guard] : We'll ride the downs at dusk. They use the old tracks, the cowards.
b : Six! That's a winter's living. | A dozen! | East, toward the drovers' road.
a : A whole winter. | Gone in a night. | Easy to sell there.

scene et_wm_arrest_frontier
when topic=crime kind=arrest region=larkfield
a : They've locked {subject} in the old watch house. | {subject}'s taken. Larkfield looks after its own, and deals with its own. | The general store pressed charges on {subject}, I hear.
b : That watch house leaks. Good. | We do. | The general store presses everyone.
a : Very good. | Always have. | Half the downs owes it.

scene et_wm_death_barrows
when topic=life kind=death region=larkfield
a : They'll lay {subject} by the old barrows. With the ancestors. | Lights on the barrows the night {subject} died. I saw them. | {subject}'s gone. The downs feel emptier.
b[old] : The barrows take their own. Always have, long before the chapel.
b[priest] : The Bright One keeps them, not the barrows. But I'll say the words there.
b : With the old ones. Right. | You saw shepherds' fires. | They do.
a : Right and proper. | I know what I saw. | Wide and empty.

scene et_wm_newcomer_frontier
when topic=newcomer region=larkfield
a : {subject} rode in from the north. Says they want land. | {subject}'s a city wolf. You can tell by the boots. | {subject} asked about the barrows. First thing.
b[herder] : Land's cheap out here. Keeping it is the hard part.
b : Plenty of it. Not much but grass. | They'll have mud on them by sundown. | Tell them to stay off them.
a : Grass, mostly. | And blisters. | I did.

scene et_wm_festival_drovers
when topic=festival region=larkfield
a : The drovers time their run to be here for {festival}. | Bonfires on every hill of the downs for {festival}. | The Singing Lark stays open all night for {festival}.
b[innkeeper] : I'll sleep after {festival}. Some time next week.
b : Cattle and ale. Larkfield feasting. | You can see them for leagues. | It always does.
a : The best kind. | Like stars on the ground. | All night.

scene et_wm_gossip
when topic=gossip region=larkfield
a : Out on the downs they're saying {subject} {claim}. | The drovers swear {subject} {claim}. | At the general store's counter: {subject} {claim}.
b : Not much else to talk about out there. | Drovers swear about everything. | The counter's where truth goes to die.
a : Sheep and gossip. | Mostly cattle. | And ledgers.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Coldwater

scene et_ls_theft_boat
when topic=crime kind=theft region=coldwater
a : Somebody's been taking boats at night again. {victim}'s this time. | {victim} lost the whole catch off the racks. | They took {victim}'s nets right off the jetty.
b[fisher] : Mist hides a thief better than any cloak.
b : The mist covers everything. | The whole catch? | Jetty's never watched.
a : Everything. | Every fish. | It is now.

scene et_ls_death_mere
when topic=life kind=death region=coldwater
a : The lake took {subject}. Went out in the mist. Never came back. | They found {subject}'s skiff drifting by the reeds. | {subject}'s gone. Glasswater's still as glass, like nothing happened.
b[fisher] : The lake's calm until it isn't. Every fisher knows it.
b : The mist. Always the mist. | Empty, I suppose. | It doesn't care. It's water.
a : Always. | Empty. | It doesn't.

scene et_ls_newcomer_garrison
when topic=newcomer region=coldwater
a : {subject} came up from the lowlands. Says they're staying. | {subject} wants to learn boatbuilding. | {subject} came in on a cart and never went back down.
b[old] : They come for the quiet. Then the winter finds them.
b : Plenty like that. | A good trade. | Running from something?
a : Plenty. | It is. | Or just tired.

scene et_ls_festival_lanterns
when topic=festival region=coldwater
a : Lanterns floating on Glasswater for {festival}. One for every soul lost. | The fishers row in from every cove for {festival}. Every year. | Boat races across the lake for {festival}!
b[child] : Can I light a lantern? Can I push it out?
b : It's beautiful. And sad. | They drink us dry. | My cousin's rowing!
a : Both. | Always. | Good luck to them.

scene et_ls_gossip
when topic=gossip region=coldwater
a : The fishers swear {subject} {claim}. | On the jetty this morning: {subject} {claim}. | Mist and whispers. {subject} {claim}.
b : Fishers. They'll say anything. | The jetty hears everything. | Fits the weather.
a : Anything. | Everything. | It does.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Mirebridge

scene et_fh_theft_cures
when topic=crime kind=theft region=mirebridge
a : Somebody stole {victim}'s dried bogmyrtle. A season's cures. | Peat stolen off the stacks. Who steals peat? | {victim} was robbed on the fen road at dusk.
b[healer] : They'll poison themselves with it if they don't know the dose.
b : A season's work. | Somebody cold. | The fen road's lonely at dusk.
a : All gone. | Cold and shameless. | Very lonely.

scene et_fh_death_marsh
when topic=life kind=death region=mirebridge
a : {subject} followed the marsh lights. They found them in the bog. | Fever took {subject}. The fen fever. | They're burying {subject} on the dry rise behind the chapel.
b[old] : Never follow the lights. My grandmother said it, and her grandmother.
b : Never follow the lights. | That fever's cruel. | Only dry ground left.
a : Never. | So cruel. | And not much of it.

scene et_fh_newcomer_cure
when topic=newcomer region=mirebridge
a : {subject} came for the marsh cures and decided to stay. | {subject} wants to learn the herbs. Brave, in this damp. | {subject} came in by the fen road, soaked to the knees.
b[healer] : I'll teach them. The fen gives as much as it takes.
b : The cures work, some of them. | They'll grow webbed paws. | Everyone does, first time.
a : Some. | Ha! | Every time.

scene et_fh_festival
when topic=festival region=mirebridge
a : They burn peat bonfires for {festival}. Smoke for a week. | Reed crowns for {festival}! I'm weaving mine. | The river bank's lined with torches for {festival}.
b[child] : My crown's bigger than yours!
b : Smells like home. | Show me when it's done. | Pretty, on the water.
a : Smoky home. | Soon. | Reflections everywhere.

scene et_fh_gossip
when topic=gossip region=mirebridge
a : Bogmyrtle says {subject} {claim}. She's never wrong. | At the peat cutting: {subject} {claim}. | Damp talk, but they say {subject} {claim}.
b : Bogmyrtle's wrong half the time. | Peat cutters gossip like crows. | Everything's damp here.
a : Never to her face. | Worse. | Even the talk.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Southmeadow

scene et_af_theft_grain
when topic=crime kind=theft region=southmeadow
a : Somebody broke into the granary. {victim}'s grain. | Grain sacks gone from {victim}'s barn. In a drought! | They took the toll box from the gate.
b[farmer] : A thief in a dry year's worse than a thief in a wet one.
b[official] : The toll box! That's the watch's wages.
b : The granary! In this drought? | Shameless. | The whole box?
a : Shameless. | Utterly. | Every penny.

scene et_af_death
when topic=life kind=death region=southmeadow
a : {subject} died in the fields. Heat took them. | They found {subject} in the millpond. The water's so low, how? | {subject}'s gone. They'll be buried under the old oak.
b[farmer] : The sun's no friend this year.
b : This heat'll kill us all. | Low water still drowns. | The oak's seen a lot of us off.
a : It might. | Always does. | It has.

scene et_af_newcomer
when topic=newcomer region=southmeadow
a : {subject} came to help with the harvest. Says they'll stay. | {subject} asked to rent a field. In a drought. | New wolf at the mill. {subject}.
b[farmer] : Strong back? Then welcome.
b : Good. We need paws. | Brave or foolish. | The miller needed help.
a : We do. | Foolish. | Good.

scene et_af_festival_harvest
when topic=festival region=southmeadow
a : The last sheaf goes on the chapel door for {festival}. | Barn dance for {festival}! | The miller's grinding sweet flour for the {festival} loaves.
b[farmer] : Even in a dry year, we feast. That's the point.
b : Good luck for the year. | I'll bring my fiddle. | Golden loaves.
a : It needs it. | Please do. | Sweet ones.

scene et_af_gossip
when topic=gossip region=southmeadow
a : At the mill they're saying {subject} {claim}. | Over the hedgerow: {subject} {claim}. | The toll-keeper says {subject} {claim}.
b : The mill's worse than a tavern. | Hedges have ears. | Toll-keepers see everyone.
a : Dustier, too. | Long ones. | And tell everyone.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Oakhaven

scene et_hm_theft
when topic=crime kind=theft region=oakhaven
a : A thief? In Oakhaven? {victim}, of all wolves. | Nobody steals in Oakhaven. And yet {victim}'s robbed. | Must be someone passing through. Nobody here would rob {victim}.
b[old] : Six generations, and I never locked my door. Now this.
b : Strange days. | And yet. | Must be.
a : Strange. | It's wrong. | Must be.

scene et_hm_life
when topic=life region=oakhaven
a : The whole town knows about {subject} by now. | {subject}! Did you hear? Of course you did. | News travels slow under the trees, except about {subject}.
b : It's a small town. | Course I did. | That's the only news.
a : Small and nosy. | Course you did. | Only news all {season}.

scene et_hm_newcomer
when topic=newcomer region=oakhaven
a : {subject} came in through the Warmwood. Nobody comes to Oakhaven by accident. | A newcomer! {subject}! First this {season}. | {subject} asked if the carter comes often.
b[old] : The last newcomer I liked was my wife. Forty years back.
b : Then why did they come? | About time! | Ha. Did you tell them the truth?
a : We'll find out. | Long past time. | I told them to be patient.

scene et_hm_festival
when topic=festival region=oakhaven
a : Just us and a fiddle for {festival}. Best kind of feast. | The whole town eats together under the oaks for {festival}. | Bonfire by the brook for {festival}.
b : The very best. | Every family brings a dish. | The brook sings for it.
a : Small and warm. | And everybody eats. | It does.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- The Ridgemere Watch

scene et_ft_gossip
when topic=gossip region=ridgemere a.job=guard
a : On the wall last night they said {subject} {claim}. | The carter at the South Gate says {subject} {claim}. | Watch House talk. {subject} {claim}.
b : Bored guards. | Carters gossip like old women. | Watch House talk is Watch House talk.
a : Very bored. | Worse. | It passes the night.
